/* ===================== *
 *    Skullbreaker          *
 * ===================== */
@201 = ~skullbreaker~
@202 = ~Skullbreaker~
@203 = ~Skullbreaker:

The Skullbreaker is a brutal warrior trained to disable foes with blunt and spiked weapons. Each weapon in their arsenal delivers a distinct crippling effect, allowing the Skullbreaker to adapt to changing battles with crushing precision.

Advantages:
- Apply a random effect each time you hit a target with a blunt melee weapon:
    - -3 penalty to AC
    - frighten target for 1 round
    - briefly stun the target
    - deal 10 additional crushing damage

- Slings have a chance to briefly stun hit targets

- May use the Shockwave ability once per day, gains an additional use every 4 levels thereafter

Shockwave:
All enemies within 15 feet are propelled back and stunned for 1 round on a failed save vs death. Huge creatures are stunned 
only momentarily and will not be knocked back.

- 10th level: The Skullbreaker becomes immune to stun and knockback effects
- 15th level: May use the Crushing Victory ability once per day

Crushing Victory:
With every ounce of strength committed to a relentless assault, the Skullbreaker strikes with enough force to splinter shields and crush armor.
All crushing damage within the next 5 rounds is doubled. When the effect ends, the Skullbreaker becomes Winded for 2 rounds and suffers a -2 penalty 
to THAC0 and armor class and 50% reduction in movement speed

Disadvantages:
- May only use 1-handed blunt melee weapons and slings and may not exceed Mastery (3 pips) in weapon proficiencies
- Alignment restricted to non-good~  